<title>FINLAND: SAK SAYS EMU GOOD IF LOW INFLATION ACCEPTED - PAPER.</title>
<headline>SAK SAYS EMU GOOD IF LOW INFLATION ACCEPTED - PAPER.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Central Organisation of Finnish Trade Unions (SAK) said EMU membership could be an economic success if Finland adjusted to moderate inflation, daily Helsingin Sanomat reported on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;If Finns adjust to moderate inflation and, in addition, buffer funds are created -- Finnish membership of the European economic and monetary union (EMU) could prove to be an economically successful decision,&quot; Helsingin Sanomat quoted SAK as saying in a report due to be published on Monday.</p>
<p>But if the moderate inflation criterion is not strictly followed it would be wise for Finland to not join EMU in the first group, SAK said.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-9-680 50 240, news@Reuters.fi</p>
